From 8f0ad1d09c366e936e9f63dedf8ad1c80453b871 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:44:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Skip the net_inflow testset until an Oceananigans release has
 NetInflow (#6524)

NestedModels' net_inflow uses Oceananigans' NetInflow and net_inflow_value, which CliMA/Oceananigans.jl#6524 adds; CI
installs a registered Oceananigans without them, so this testset fails with UndefVarError. Guard it on
isdefined(Oceananigans.BoundaryConditions, :NetInflow) until #6524 is released.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AbhhvpKgDchWb93a6aYpaq
---
 test/test_nested_ocean_model.jl | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/test/test_nested_ocean_model.jl b/test/test_nested_ocean_model.jl
index 81b9dce6..dd06ae4c 100644
--- a/test/test_nested_ocean_model.jl
+++ b/test/test_nested_ocean_model.jl
@@ -526,6 +526,8 @@ end
     end
 end
 
+# TODO: drop the guard once an Oceananigans release has `NetInflow` (CliMA/Oceananigans.jl#6524)
+isdefined(Oceananigans.BoundaryConditions, :NetInflow) &&
 @testset "net_inflow pins the net inflow through the open sides together on $(arch)" for arch in test_architectures
     # The parent's u = 0.1 m/s brings about 22 Sv in through the west side; ask for 2 Sv in through both sides together,
     # then for 1 Sv out
-- 
